BR2_PACKAGE_STEAM_DEVICES=y
BR2_PACKAGE_GAMEMODE=y

# --- Services behind portals Flatpak apps already see (2026-10-11) -------------
# - rtkit (our package): the Realtime portal forwards to RealtimeKit; without it
#   audio workstations, games, voice chat and PipeWire inside a sandbox got no
#   realtime threads (xdg-desktop-portal: "Failed to load RealtimeKit property").
# - geoclue (our package): the Location portal is compiled into
#   xdg-desktop-portal only with libgeoclue. Maps, weather, browsers and COSMIC
#   Settings' sunset-based dark mode had no location.
# - v4l2loopback: OBS's virtual camera (and any "fake webcam" tool) needs this
#   kernel module, which a Flatpak cannot bring. OBS loads it on demand with
#   pkexec; modprobe.d/60-pengyos-v4l2loopback.conf gives it OBS's options.
#   (Buildroot's recipe only turns MEDIA_SUPPORT/VIDEO_DEV on when unset; our
#   =m stays.)
# - glib-networking: GIO's TLS backend (gnutls here). Without it every libsoup
#   or GIO client failed HTTPS with "TLS support is not available": geoclue's
#   BeaconDB lookups, and gvfs's dav/http backends (COSMIC Files' davs://, e.g.
