# image found these missing. Each one turned a COSMIC feature into a no-op:
# - rfkill: the Bluetooth applet and Settings block/unblock the adapter with it;
#   after airplane mode the toggle could not bring Bluetooth back.
# - pactl: cosmic-settings-daemon sends Mono Audio to pipewire-pulse and sets
#   virtual sinks/sources as default with it; PulseAudio-protocol apps (every
#   Flatpak browser, Discord, Spotify) stayed stereo. PulseAudio is built
#   client-only (external.mk: no daemon, which would fight pipewire-pulse for
#   the socket): libpulse and pactl.
# - qalc (libqalculate, our package): the launcher's "= 2+2" calculator.
# - notify-send (libnotify, our package): notifications from scripts.
BR2_PACKAGE_UTIL_LINUX_RFKILL=y
BR2_PACKAGE_PULSEAUDIO=y
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBQALCULATE=y
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBNOTIFY=y

